config BR2_PACKAGE_MAJESTIC_AF
	bool "majestic-af"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_MAJESTIC
	help
	  Out-of-core motor driver and autofocus engine for majestic, compiled
	  from source. majestic loads /usr/lib/majestic-af.so at runtime when a
	  motorized lens is declared and the majestic binary exports the plugin
	  HAL seams; the contrast search, the motorized-lens actuators, and the
	  worker threads live here. Two actuator families are implemented: a UART
	  wire for the XiongMai near-Pelco and standard Pelco-D lenses, and an
	  MS41908M SPI stepper (isp.autofocus.actuator=ms41908) for the Hi3516A/D
	  V100 boards whose zoom/focus lens is on SPI with no UART lens MCU.

	  For the UART families it is the ONLY writer on that tty, and it is now
	  required for manual PTZ as well as autofocus: the WebUI asks majestic
	  for a verb over its HTTP API rather than shipping its own Pelco scripts,
	  which used to open the same tty behind the daemon's back. A camera with
	  ptz_control=pelco-d or pelco-xm and no driver keeps its pad but says
	  what is missing, rather than claiming the camera has no PTZ.

	  https://github.com/OpenIPC/majestic-af
